arm64: dts: rockchip: build the CX3576-Z device tree

kernel/dts/rk3576-cx3576z.dts is this board's maintained device tree and the
Makefile in the pinned Armbian tree does not know about it. Registering it is
what makes `make rockchip/rk3576-cx3576z.dtb` produce anything.

This replaces an `echo ... >> arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile` that the
Dockerfile ran between two build steps (RFCT-343). A patch is the same edit
stated where every other source change to this tree is stated -- reviewable in
a diff, applied by the same series with the same reject handling, and counted
by the same series-length assertion -- instead of a shell redirection whose
failure mode is an append that silently lands in the wrong file.

The line goes with the other `dtb-` entries rather than after `subdir-y`, which
is where the append put it. That is a placement change and not a behaviour
change: the variable is accumulated, so the built dtb is byte-identical either
way, and RFCT-343's recorded rk3576-src.dtb hash is the control.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile
@@ -463,4 +463,5 @@
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3566-roc-pc.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3576-recomputer-rk3576-devkit.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588-recomputer-rk3588-devkit.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3576-cx3576z.dtb
 subdir-y := $(dts-dirs) overlay
